Subject: [PATCH] fix(skills): map capabilities to setup guidance

---
 .agents/skills/setup/SKILL.md             | 34 ++++++++++++++---------
 .agents/skills/setup/evals/scorecard.json |  8 +++---
 skills/coverage.json                      |  1 +
 skills/setup/SKILL.md                     | 34 ++++++++++++++---------
 skills/setup/evals/scorecard.json         |  8 +++---
 5 files changed, 51 insertions(+), 34 deletions(-)

diff --git a/.agents/skills/setup/SKILL.md b/.agents/skills/setup/SKILL.md
index d71d6206..2ef884ec 100644
--- a/.agents/skills/setup/SKILL.md
+++ b/.agents/skills/setup/SKILL.md
@@ -1,18 +1,15 @@
 ---
 name: setup
 description: >
-  Forge install & setup lifecycle. `forge setup` interactively configures Forge for your
-  coding agents; `forge init [--profile minimal|standard|full]` writes the
-  adoption config in a fresh repo; `forge doctor` reports whether the kernel DB is on a
-  cloud/network path; `forge upgrade [--dry-run]` previews + self-heals upgrade readiness;
-  `forge hooks install --global` installs native hooks; `forge reset --soft|--hard --force`
-  and `forge reinstall --force` undo/redo the install; `forge recommend` lists suggested
-  tools. Use when the user says "install/set up forge", "init forge", "adoption profile",
-  "forge doctor", "upgrade forge", "install the hooks globally", or "reset/reinstall forge".
-  Footguns: setup is interactive — pass `--yes` in automation; `doctor` only checks the
-  kernel-DB filesystem class, NOT general health; `upgrade` self-heals Forge state, NOT the
-  npm package; reset/reinstall need `--force`. NOT toggling a gate/rail (gates), NOT
-  orienting in a set-up repo (status), NOT installing project deps (dev).
+  Forge install and setup lifecycle. Configure agents with `forge setup`; initialize an adoption
+  profile with `forge init`; diagnose the installation with `forge doctor`; report installed
+  products and behavior-probed harness support with `forge capabilities --json`; preview repairs
+  with `forge upgrade`; install global hooks; reset or reinstall; and recommend tools. Use when the user asks
+  "install Forge", "set up Forge", "adoption profile", "Forge doctor", "what capabilities are
+  available", "upgrade Forge", "install hooks globally", or "reset Forge". Setup is interactive,
+  so pass `--yes` in automation. Scoped Doctor checks fail closed while its default preserves
+  legacy exit behavior. Not for gate toggles (gates), project work state (status), or project
+  dependencies (dev).
 allowed-tools: Bash, Read, Grep, Glob
 terminal: true
 ---
@@ -65,7 +62,18 @@ forge doctor            # is the kernel DB on a cloud-synced / network path? (re
 forge doctor --json     # machine-readable
 ```
 
-`forge doctor` is **narrow**: it reports the filesystem class of the Forge kernel database path (local / cloud-synced / network) so you can catch the reliability footgun of running the DB on OneDrive/Dropbox/a network share. It is **not** a general health check.
+`forge doctor` keeps its legacy filesystem result while the manifest-driven report also checks
+the requested Health scope. An unavailable or malformed explicitly requested check fails closed;
+optional product checks do not change the legacy default exit behavior.
+
+Inspect installed products and behavior-probed harness support without activating them:
+
+```bash
+forge capabilities --json
+```
+
+Treat unprobed, stale, or unavailable capabilities as unavailable. The report does not infer
+semantic support from a harness name or help text.
 
 # Upgrade readiness
 
